{
  "dom_id": "step-e12796",
  "name": "Example: Simplifying Expressions With Four Terms",
  "problem": "Simplify the expression $5k - 3k + 2k - t.$",
  "worked_solution": "We have three like terms, $5k, -3k,$ and $2k.$ \n\nTo collect these like terms, we combine them into a single term, adding their coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5k-3k+2k-t & = \\\\ (5-3+2)k-t & = \\\\ 4k-t\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
